## Rollback Procedures

### 1. Rollback Strategy

**Preparation:**
- Maintain previous versions
- Test rollback in staging
- Document rollback process
- Set rollback time limits
- Monitor after rollback

**Triggers for Rollback:**
- Increased error rate
- Failed health checks
- Performance degradation
- Failed smoke tests
- Customer reports

### 2. Database Rollback

**Challenges:**
- Data might have changed
- Schema changes are harder to revert
- May need data migration

**Strategies:**
- Avoid destructive migrations
- Maintain backwards compatibility
- Use feature flags to disable features
- Restore from backup (last resort)

## Disaster Recovery

### 1. Backup Strategy

**What to Backup:**
- Database (regular automated backups)
- Application configuration
- User-uploaded files
- Secrets and certificates
- Infrastructure configuration

**Backup Types:**
- Full backups (weekly)
- Incremental backups (daily)
- Continuous backups (transaction logs)

**Backup Testing:**
- Regular restore tests
- Document restore procedure
- Measure Recovery Time Objective (RTO)
- Measure Recovery Point Objective (RPO)

### 2. Disaster Recovery Plan

**Components:**
- Backup and restore procedures
- Failover procedures
- Communication plan
- Roles and responsibilities
- Post-incident review process

## Performance and Scaling

### 1. Horizontal vs. Vertical Scaling

**Horizontal (Scale Out):**
- Add more instances
- Better for stateless applications
- Requires load balancing
- More resilient

**Vertical (Scale Up):**
- Increase resources per instance
- Simpler to implement
- Hardware limitations
- Single point of failure

### 2. Load Balancing

**Load Balancer Types:**
- Layer 4 (Transport): TCP/UDP
- Layer 7 (Application): HTTP/HTTPS

**Load Balancing Algorithms:**
- Round Robin
- Least Connections
- IP Hash
- Weighted distribution

### 3. Caching Strategy

**Cache Layers:**
- CDN (static assets)
- Application cache (Redis, Memcached)
- Database query cache
- HTTP cache headers

**Cache Invalidation:**
- Time-based (TTL)
- Event-based
- Manual invalidation
- Cache-aside pattern

## Security in Deployment

### 1. Supply Chain Security

- Scan dependencies for vulnerabilities
- Pin dependency versions
- Use private registries
- Sign and verify artifacts
- Regular security updates

### 2. Runtime Security

- Run containers as non-root
- Read-only file systems
- Drop unnecessary capabilities
- Network policies
- Secret management
- Regular security scans

### 3. Access Control

- Principle of least privilege
- Role-based access (RBAC)
- Multi-factor authentication
- Audit logs
- Regular access reviews

